title: Disco in Six
key: D
tempo: 116
meter: 6/8
style: disco

// The floor in six-eight: two pulses to the bar, three eighths in each, at the
// dancer's speed, so a bar is a second long and most chords last two. Thirty-two
// bars. The verse goes from the one to its two-five, then down to the six and a
// two-five a pulse each; the second verse turns through the three and the five
// of two. The chorus opens on the four, steps down through the three to the six,
// goes to the two and rests on the suspended five, goes round again by the five
// of two, and comes home by the two-five.
[Verse]
| Dmaj9 | % | Em7 | A13     |
| Dmaj9 | % | Bm9 | Em7 A13 |

[Verse 2]
| Dmaj9 | %  | Em7 | A13 |
| F#m7  | B7 | Em7 | A13 |

[Chorus]
| Gmaj9 | %   | F#m7   | Bm9 |
| Em7   | %   | A9sus4 | A13 |
| Gmaj9 | %   | F#m7   | B7  |
| Em7   | A13 | Dmaj9  | A13 |
